# LIBRARY: own
# A method that the class declares is found without a lookup if the cell still has the prototype of its layout.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeGuardsAndFacts: the planner of typed accesses assumes that every class guard holds and that every cell fact has been established, and it leaves the state untouched.
# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks), what the access relies on is checked where nothing has established it, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: of the class
# RIGHT-NEXT: from above
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HARDENED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HARDENED: of the class
# HARDENED-NEXT: from above
# HARDENED-NEXT: exited with 0
